                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "some bycatch from testing:\n\nwe are missing the `io.stop()` here in the error case, right?\n\nfound this by accident and had to ctrl-c the process.\n\n```\nroot@s8030-bmc-30303035c0c1:~# bmcweb loglevel debug\n<3>[webserver_cli.cpp:72] SetLogLevel returned error with No route to host [generic:113]\n^C\n```\n\nThe loglevel setting failure on my system is probably unrelated to this patch here\nso making this comment as resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 73,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes we do appear to be.  We really should be implementing a shudown on the connection and letting the io_service stop itself once the connection has closed, but that's not what's implemented today\n\nAlso capturing loglevel by reference is wrong and could be use after free."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 73,
